\c orcid

--
-- Liquibase's record of how the schema in 4-orcid-schema.sql got here.
--
-- The app runs Liquibase at startup: orcid-persistence-context.xml declares a
-- SpringLiquibase bean over db-master.xml, and both entityManagerFactory beans
-- depend on it, so it is not optional. Liquibase decides what to apply by
-- reading this table. An EMPTY databasechangelog is not "no history" to it --
-- it means "nothing has ever been applied", so on first boot it replays the
-- entire changelog against the schema 4-orcid-schema.sql just created. Most
-- changesets survive that on their onFail="MARK_RAN" preconditions; twenty-one
-- of the sixty-nine that create a table carry none, and the first of those
-- fails the deployment outright:
--
--   Migration failed for db/updates/0.2.xml::ADD-TABLE-FOR-DELEGATION-OF-PERMISSIONS
--   Reason: ERROR: relation "given_permission_to" already exists
--
-- These rows say the schema is current, so Liquibase applies nothing and a
-- fresh database boots. Regenerate them alongside the schema with
-- docker-compose-dump-schema.sh; the two must come from the same database or
-- they will disagree about what has been applied.
--

